<title>CANADA: Gandalf seeks creditor protection, buyer.</title>
<headline>Gandalf seeks creditor protection, buyer.</headline>
<dateline>KANATA, Ontario 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Beleaguered Gandalf Technologies Inc said on Friday that it had filed for creditor protection to allow it to reorganize and perhaps find a buyer.  </p>
<p>The telecommunications equipment maker, based outside Ottawa, said it would restructure and reorganize under the Companies' Creditors Arrangement Act (CCAA). Creditors would be unable to claim their debts until after October 31, it said.</p>
<p>Gandalf added that it cut its North American staff by 180 today. &quot;This restructuring is intended to enable continued operations on a more economically viable basis to allow the opportunity for the company to continue seeking an investor or a partner to acquire all or part of Gandalf,&quot; it said in a long-awaited statement.</p>
</text>
